==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|fr|chandelle|t=chandelle}}. {{doublet|en|candela|candle}}.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# An [[aerobatic]] [[maneuver]] in which a 180° [[turn]] is combined with a [[climb]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Flight Maneuvers|page=190|author=Michael Charles Love|year=1998|passage=The FAA terms a '''chandelle''' as a maximum fight performance maneuver. During the course of a '''chandelle''' the plane should gain the greatest amount of altitude possible for a given degree of bank, and without stalling.}}

